<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico assigns first direct cetes sale.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico assigns first direct cetes sale.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico assigned the first of three direct sales of paper and five repurchase agreements whereby it had sought to drain 2.956 billion pesos from the secondary market on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sale was placed as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    338 days   22.91 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    177 days</p>
<p>    150 million     86 days</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements offered were as follows:</p>
<p>    550 million     34 days</p>
<p>    550 million     23 days</p>
<p>    550 million     16 days</p>
<p>    550 million     13 days</p>
<p>    306 million	1 day</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9554))</p>
